# rule: hid_then_shell
# platform: Elastic EQL sequence
# index: usb-monitoring (raw or normalized)
# schedule: from now-6m, interval 5m
# MITRE: T1200 — Hardware Additions; T1059.001 — PowerShell
# expected alert shape: one sequence per host with a HID connect followed by
#   powershell.exe/cmd.exe within 60 seconds
# caveats:
#   - Attach an exception list keyed on the device identifier (serial or device
#     instance path); do not hardcode example values.
#   - Sysmon does not log USB connects. Security 6416 can log HID when Audit
#     PnP Activity is enabled, but HID serials are often absent/non-unique.
#   - Do not enable until the HID source and identifier quality are validated.
#   - Secondary Elastic translation; see appendix/elastic/README.md.
sequence by host.name with maxspan=60s
  [any where event.code : "6416" and usb.device_class == "HID"]
  [any where event.type : "start" and process.name : ("powershell.exe" or "cmd.exe")]
